course: dictionary
lesson: 3483
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Family» is a good example. Most of the time it means the people you are related to, like parents and their children.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Some children are adopted: they join a family that did not give birth to them, and they are just as much part of it.» Here family means the people you belong to and live with, even if they are not related by birth.
explain: Other clues point to other meanings. «The cat family» means a group of animals that are alike, such as lions and tigers. «You're like family» means close friends. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence best?
fact: Family means a group of people who are related, like parents and their children.
fact: Family can also mean all your relatives, such as aunts, uncles, cousins and grandparents.
fact: In science, a family is a group of animals or plants that are alike, as in «the cat family».
fact: Casually, «fam» or «family» can mean close friends.
fact: A more formal word for the people in a home is «household», as in «members of the household».
exercise: «Older children in big families often help a lot, but they still need breakfast, sleep and time for themselves.» In this sentence, what does families mean? | *A group of people who are related, and who share a home | A football team | A group of animals that are alike | A group of people who are related
exercise: In «the cat family», what does family mean? | A group of close friends | A group of people who are related | *A group of animals that are alike | A house with a garden
exercise: Which formal word means the people who live together in one home? | playground | cousin | *household | fam
test: «If Gran says "keep the change", telling her how much is left makes it an honest gift; being open about money stops mix-ups in families.» What does families mean here? | Animals that look alike | Close friends only | Teams that play sport | *People who are related or who live together
test: «You're like family to me, fam.» What does family mean here? | Relatives who are aunts and uncles only | *Close friends | A household of four persons, counted in a form | A group of animals
exam: Which meaning of family fits «the cat family»? | *A group of animals or plants that are alike | A group of close friends | A formal word for a home | Relatives such as aunts and uncles
